Third-party software that this repository does not contain
----------------------------------------------------------

The build links Roboception's GenICam SDK rc_genicam_api, which you install
separately (https://github.com/roboception/rc_genicam_api). According to the
SDK's LICENSE.md (checked with version 2.8.9):

- The files in its directories rc_genicam_api and tools are provided by
  Roboception GmbH under the 3-clause BSD licence.
- Its directory genicam contains the GenICam reference implementation of the
  EMVA and contributors, under the licences in genicam/License_ReadMe.txt and
  genicam/licenses/ (the GenICam licence and those of third-party packages).
- Its directory baumer contains a GenTL producer for GigE Vision from Baumer
  Optronic GmbH, under Baumer's licence agreement in baumer/license.txt.

A binary distribution of this node that includes the SDK's libraries must
carry those licence texts.
